= Informational inheritance =

== Overview ==
'''Informational inheritance''' is the transmission, persistence or reconstruction of informationally structured constraints, records or states from an earlier system, generation or process to a later one. The phrase is used here as a '''comparative systems concept''', not as one universally standardized biological or computational mechanism.

To study inheritance precisely, identify '''what is transmitted''', '''the carrier''', '''the mechanism of transfer or reconstruction''', '''how changes arise''', '''how fidelity is assessed''', and '''whether the recipient has the same identity as the source'''. Transmission does not require identity preservation.

